# App wallpaper (circles)

Every screen uses the shared canvas from
[`AppWallpaper`](lib/core/ui/widgets/app_wallpaper.dart) — surface fill,
primary/secondary blobs, and a light grid. It is dual-theme (Material roles).

## Standard screens (`CurvedAppBarLayout`)

Do **not** wrap the wallpaper yourself. [`CurvedAppBarLayout`](lib/core/ui/widgets/curved_app_bar.dart)
already paints `AppWallpaper` behind the body and bar.

```dart
Scaffold(
  backgroundColor: Colors.transparent,
  body: CurvedAppBarLayout(
    appBar: CurvedAppBar(title: S.current.homePage, showDrawerMenu: true),
    body: _Content(),
  ),
)
```

- Set `Scaffold.backgroundColor` to `Colors.transparent` so the circles show
- Do **not** stack a second `AppWallpaper` around `CurvedAppBarLayout`
- Opt out only when the canvas is fully replaced (e.g. a full-bleed map):
  `CurvedAppBarLayout(..., showWallpaper: false)`

## Onboarding / splash (no curved bar)

Place wallpaper as the first child of a full-screen `Stack`:

```dart
Scaffold(
  backgroundColor: Colors.transparent,
  body: Stack(
    fit: StackFit.expand,
    children: [
      const AppWallpaper(),
      SafeArea(child: _Content()),
    ],
  ),
)
```

## Do / don't

```dart
// ❌ BAD — opaque scaffold hides the circles
backgroundColor: Theme.of(context).scaffoldBackgroundColor,

// ❌ BAD — duplicate wallpaper on a CurvedAppBarLayout screen
Stack(children: [const AppWallpaper(), CurvedAppBarLayout(...)])

// ✅ GOOD — layout paints it
body: CurvedAppBarLayout(appBar: CurvedAppBar(title: ...), body: ...),
```
